10. Create and Explore exam_data
Aim

To create and manipulate a data frame named exam_data by extracting data, adding rows and columns, sorting and saving it to a file.

Procedure
Create a data frame with name, score, attempts and qualify.
Display its structure.
Extract required rows and columns.
Add a new row and column.
Sort the data.
Save the data frame as a CSV file.
Code
# Create data frame
exam_data <- data.frame(
  name=c("Arun","Bala","Chitra","Divya","Elan"),
  score=c(85,72,91,65,78),
  attempts=c(1,2,1,3,2),
  qualify=c(TRUE,TRUE,TRUE,FALSE,TRUE)
)

# Display data
print(exam_data)

# Structure
str(exam_data)

# Extract score
print(exam_data$score)

# Extract first row
print(exam_data[1,])

