12. Data Reshaping Using Melt and Cast
Aim

To reshape an air-quality dataset using melt and cast operations and calculate monthly averages of Ozone, Solar Radiation, Wind and Temperature.

Procedure
Load the airquality dataset.
Load the reshape2 package.
Convert the data into long format using melt().
Convert it into summarized wide format using dcast().
Calculate monthly averages.
Code
# Install once if required:
# install.packages("reshape2")

library(reshape2)

# Load airquality dataset
data <- airquality

# Melt data
melted <- melt(
  data,
  id.vars=c("Month","Day"),
  measure.vars=c("Ozone","Solar.R","Wind","Temp")
)

print(melted)

# Cast data and calculate monthly averages
casted <- dcast(
  melted,
  Month ~ variable,
  fun.aggregate=mean,
  na.rm=TRUE
)

print(casted)

# Monthly averages
monthly_avg <- aggregate(
  cbind(Ozone, Solar.R, Wind, Temp) ~ Month,
  data=data,
  FUN=mean,
  na.rm=TRUE
)

print(monthly_avg)
Result

Thus, the air-quality dataset was reshaped using melt and cast operations and monthly averages were calculated successfully.

